{title: Infant Holy, Infant Lowly}
{artist: Polish carol · tr. Edith Reed}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 76}

Verse 1
[F]Infant holy, infant lowly, [C]for his bed a [F]cattle stall;
oxen lowing, little knowing [C]Christ the babe is [F]Lord of all.
[Bb]Swift are winging [F]angels singing, [Bb]noels ringing, [F]tidings bringing:
[C]Christ the babe is [F]Lord of all.
